Your usage limit was reached early in this task, so none of the 42 cases is fixed and nothing changed in either repository. I have not created a worktree, a commit or any code. What I did produce is the list of decisions Kenneth needs to make, findings for three cases, and a hand-over note so the next session can start from them.

**Rule text.** The new error-handling text landed while I worked. It is now on `jusprin-dev` (9f485c3604) and tsd-enterprise `master` (d9c224e114), and both open with "Someone pastes a key from their own AI service". New branches should start from those commits.

**Decisions for Kenneth.** These are written out as full "Decision needed" paragraphs in `misrouted-failures-decisions.md` in the shared notes folder, and I've sent your session a pointer to them. Each has options, what each costs, and my pick:
- how the app shows a service's own words (my pick: `OpenRouter says: “…”`);
- refunding a message that was charged when the AI service failed (case 41);
- whether a tool error that the AI model passes on counts as telling the person;
- what autosave does on a failure that is ours;
- what happens when a report can't be sent;
- two cases the rule doesn't place: strangers posting junk to the server's public launch address, and GitHub for the update check;
- case 27 (JusPrin 1's server code), which I'm leaving alone unless he says otherwise.

The list of new sentences of ours isn't written yet; it comes once the fixes exist.

**Findings so far.** These come from reading, one real answer and Chargebee's docs. None of the three cases has been reproduced yet.
- **Case 41, a message charged when the AI failed.** The reading confirms it. The server charges before it asks the AI service, and nothing gives the credits back. Pressing Retry also sends the message under a new turn id (`AgentHost.cpp:3280`), so the person is charged again.
- **Case 42, "credits added" with nothing granted.** This can really happen. Chargebee documents that a direct-debit payment leaves the invoice "payment due" for days. In that case `finish_checkout` still returns the full credit count, and the page says "500 credits added". It grants nothing. Not yet checked: whether the JusPrin 2 Chargebee site has direct debit turned on.
- **Case 28, own OpenRouter key told "something went wrong on our side".** The real answer behind Sentry issue JUSPRIN-APP-E is an OpenRouter 404 at Check key, with a message written for a person. I've drafted a proposed rule for what the app does with answers it has no specific handling for: show the service's words for refusals about the person's key or model, and tell the truth when the service is down. Anything that can't be told stays ours. The draft is in the hand-over note.

**What's left.**
- All 42 cases still need to be reproduced, fixed and shown fixed.
- One practical blocker: the one local server stack mounts the main tsd-enterprise checkout, so it can't run code from a worktree. A way to test worktree code without starting a second stack is still needed.

The hand-over note is `/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_cd3120f7-030a-4af8-a6d1-28ecae789f1a/misrouted-failures-handover.md`.

Sources: [Chargebee GoCardless direct debit](https://www.chargebee.com/docs/payments/2.0/gocardless.html), [Chargebee hosted pages API](https://apidocs.chargebee.com/docs/api/hosted_pages.md)

